        "type": "reasoning_text",
        "text": "Q6 answer: loop-guard has streak (consecutive identical tool calls, not failures) in-memory per turn, resets at used===1, and IDs; can be conceptually reused (\"streak\" pattern) but does not count failure semantics and is reset every turn + not persisted. delegation-receipts has outcome failed/uncertain per requestId, and countRetries/countResumes counting retry/resume attempts per ticket, not failure streak; no consecutive-fail counter, no per-domain/class grouping. work-record workSummaryFor gives failed count over last 10 per partner (used to display \"近 10 单：失败 N\") — closest to \"failure count\" but it's aggregate, includes non-consecutive, partner-scoped. So \"同类失败连续 3 次\" would need new state: fingerprint of failure class + streak, persisted (or process memory). Can reuse receipt table's pattern (request_id prefix e.g. `fail:<kind>:<n>`) or work summary parsing, but no existing consecutive mechanism. Also check if there's delegation failure classification with \"reason\" (partner-runtime 467). Let's see partner-runtime 430-490 for failure reasons categories; maybe a \"model-chain\" failure counting (unanswered). Search \"unanswered\" counting / model-chain failures."
      }
